[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3525271410","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112481#issuecomment-3525271410","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112481","id":3525271410,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SH19y","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T04:24:07Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T07:34:36Z","body":"Some preliminary testing using a modified MRP from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104194\r\n\r\n[android-4.4-perf-clay.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23515624/android-4.4-perf-clay.zip)\r\n\r\nThe original MRP has a loop that adds SubViewports that have a single Sprite rendered to them, then are rendered to the screen. \r\n\r\nThat means that in a loop of N, we rendering N * 2 draw calls using N + 1 render passes (i.e. N render passes with 1 draw call and 1 render pass with N draw calls). None of the draw calls are batched, so this MRP exposes the worst case performance. It can be CPU bottlenecked on some hardware and GPU bottlenecked on others. \r\n\r\nThe second test case renders N sprites with the same texture in the same location. This is the best case for batching. The number of draw calls depends on the hardware's capabilities, but it is often only 1 or a handful. Drawing that many Sprites in one location is a weird edge case for TBDR GPUs, so Mali GPUs and Apple silicon GPUs may not reflect typical performance scenarios. \r\n\r\n```\r\n# 2000 Sprites Adreno 530\r\n4.3: 55 FPS\r\n4.5.1: 10 FPS\r\nPR:  43 FPS\r\n\r\n# 100 viewports Adreno 530\r\n4.3 36 FPS\r\n4.5.1: 6 FPS\r\nPR: 30 FPS\r\n\r\n# 10000 Sprites Adreno 640\r\n4.3 25 FPS\r\n4.5.1: 19 FPS\r\nPR: 37 FPS\r\n\r\n# 500 viewports Adreno 640\r\n4.3 18 FPS\r\n4.5.1: 12 FPS\r\nPR: 18 FPS\r\n\r\n# 10000 Sprites Mali G715\r\n4.3 52 FPS\r\n4.5.1: 45 FPS\r\nPR: 57 FPS\r\n\r\n# 500 viewports Mali G715\r\n4.3 32 FPS\r\n4.5.1: 24 FPS\r\nPR: 25 FPS (This is likely caused by an unrelated bug and should be investigated)\r\n\r\n# 10000 Sprites Intel XE\r\n4.3: 80 FPS\r\n4.5.1: 23 FPS\r\nPR: 102 FPS\r\n\r\n# 500 viewports Intel XE\r\n4.3: 28 FPS\r\n4.5.1: 16 FPS\r\nPR: 39 FPS\r\n\r\n# 10000 Sprites Windows - Ryzen 5 9600X - Radeon RX 6900 XT\r\n4.3: 675 FPS\r\n4.5.1:  752 FPS\r\nPR: 856 FPS\r\nMaster: 839 FPS\r\n\r\n# 500 viewports Windows - Ryzen 5 9600X - Radeon RX 6900 XT\r\n4.3: 1475 FPS\r\n4.5.1:  1924 FPS\r\nPR: 2307 FPS\r\nMaster: 2206 FPS\r\n\r\n# 50000 Sprites Windows - Ryzen 5 9600X - Radeon RX 6900 XT\r\n4.3: 102 FPS\r\n4.5.1:  170 FPS\r\nPR: 145 FPS\r\nMaster: 145 FPS\r\n\r\n# 10000 viewports Windows - Ryzen 5 9600X - Radeon RX 6900 XT\r\n4.3:  97 FPS (GPU Bound)\r\n4.5.1:  13 FPS\r\nPR: 98 FP\r\nMaster: CRASH\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3525271410/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3526078312","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112481#issuecomment-3526078312","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112481","id":3526078312,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SK69o","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T07:36:02Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T07:36:02Z","body":"I can implement the D3D12 changes. Should I make a PR to your fork?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3526078312/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532610963","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112481#issuecomment-3532610963","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112481","id":3532610963,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Sj12T","user":{"login":"software-2","id":20566902,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNTY2OTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20566902?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-2","html_url":"https://github.com/software-2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T12:57:32Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T12:57:32Z","body":"I ran some tests on my Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 FE+, which seems to be a worst-case device, using my original test program ([here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104194#issuecomment-2755104452)). @clayjohn should I run your modified version? (I didn't see it until after I finished)\r\n\r\nI couldn't get this PR branch to run (the android app would hang at the splash screen). Master at bd2ca13c6f3a5198eac035c855dcd1759e077313 ran just fine, so I pulled in this PR's commits on top of that.\r\n\r\n\r\n4.5-dev3: 68-72fps lows, sometimes hitting 80\r\nmaster: 72-80 lows, but frequently hitting the device max of 90\r\nmaster + PR: 86-90 consistently, but I'm seeing dips sometimes to 74 briefly about every 10 seconds. (Those spikes seem to disappear when I have the Visual Profiler running, keeping a consistent 86+ when the profiler is on.)\r\n\r\nFor comparison, 4.3-stable (prior to the batching changes) gives lower overall frames (~82 on average), but does not have the occasional framerate dip.\r\n\r\nThis is absolutely a major improvement! ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532610963/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534113972","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112481#issuecomment-3534113972","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112481","id":3534113972,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Spky0","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T18:46:33Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T18:46:33Z","body":"> I ran some tests on my Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 FE+, which seems to be a worst-case device, using my original test program ([here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104194#issuecomment-2755104452)). @clayjohn should I run your modified version? (I didn't see it until after I finished)\r\n\r\nNo need. My modified version just added a couple lines of code to also test rendering a high number of sprites in a single batch\r\n\r\n> I couldn't get this PR branch to run (the android app would hang at the splash screen). Master at [bd2ca13](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/bd2ca13c6f3a5198eac035c855dcd1759e077313) ran just fine, so I pulled in this PR's commits on top of that.\r\n\r\nSorry about that, there was an android regression two days ago that was fixed yesterday https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112716. Pulling in this change on top of master was the right thing to do!\r\n\r\n> For comparison, 4.3-stable (prior to the batching changes) gives lower overall frames (~82 on average), but does not have the occasional framerate dip.\r\n\r\nDepending on your build settings, the dip may go away with official builds. We enable swappy by default on official builds which helps reduce frame dips. By default, swappy is disabled for custom build\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534113972/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534130567","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112481#issuecomment-3534130567","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112481","id":3534130567,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Spo2H","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","